Package: dcameaipe
Title: Estimation of Average Interactive Partial Effects (AIPE) and Difference in Conditional Average Marginal Effects (D-CAME)
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Jordi", "Serrano-Serrat",
           email = "jserranoserrat@gmail.com",
           role  = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Companion package to Serrano-Serrat,
    "The Pitfalls of Assuming Linear Treatment Effects in Interaction Tests",
    Sociological Science (2026).
    Provides the function dcame_aipe() for estimating the Average Interactive
    Partial Effect (AIPE) and the Difference in Conditional Average Marginal
    Effects (D-CAME) under flexible (polynomial / B-spline / GAM) functional
    forms for the treatment-by-moderator interaction. Supports robust and
    cluster-robust inference, survey weights, fixed effects, common-support
    trimming, cross-fit and bootstrap standard errors, and a clean comparison
    to the conventional linear interaction estimator. Produces diagnostic
    plots and export-ready tables. This package was enhanced and optimized
    using Claude Opus 4.7 and 4.8.
